@Begin

Metadata:
- Patient: Margaret, 74 years old
- Diagnosis: Early-stage Alzheimer's disease
- Language profile: Word-finding pauses, repetition, generally coherent

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Good morning, Margaret. Thank you for coming in today. Can you tell me a little bit about how you've been feeling lately? *PAT*

Margaret: (..) hi... *pauses* doctor... *clears throat* I don't know, it's just... everything seems... *pauses again*... different. *laughs nervously*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* That's okay, Margaret. It's normal to feel that way. Can you tell me what you mean by "different"? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses* um... things... *looks around the room*... I don't know... *trails off*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* It's okay, Margaret. Let's take our time. Can you think of anything specific that's been bothering you or causing you concern? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses* my... *pauses again*... husband... *looks down*... I don't know... *sighs*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* I'm so sorry to hear that, Margaret. What's wrong with your husband? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *stammers*... I... uh... *laughs nervously*... I don't know... *looks confused*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* It's okay, Margaret. We'll figure it out. Can you tell me about your husband? What's his name, and where do you live? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... my... *pauses again*... name... *stammers*... uh... *laughs nervously*... I don't know... *looks down*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Margaret, it's okay. We can work through this. Let me ask you something. What's your favorite hobby or activity? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *pauses again*... garden... *smiles slightly*... I love... uh... *trails off*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* That's great! Gardening can be very therapeutic. Do you have a favorite flower or plant that you like to grow? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *stammers*... rose... *smiles*... I love... uh... *gets up to get a nearby rose*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Ah, wonderful! Roses are very beautiful. Margaret, can you tell me about a time when you felt happy and carefree? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *pauses again*... summer... *smiles*... I love... uh... *gets up and starts walking towards the window*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Okay, Margaret, let's take a break. We can continue this conversation later. *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *looks around*... what... uh... *gets back into her chair*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Margaret, can you tell me about a person who is very important to you? Someone you feel close to? *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *pauses again*... friend... *smiles*... I love... uh... *trails off*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* That's great, Margaret. It's wonderful to have close relationships. We'll work on this and see how you're doing in the coming weeks. *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *looks down*... thank you... *smiles slightly*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* You're welcome, Margaret. We'll be in touch soon. *PAT*

Margaret: *pauses*... *gets up and walks out of the room*

Dr. Chen: *CLI* Okay... *watches as Margaret exits the room*

